---
import BaseLayout from "../layout/BaseLayout.astro"
---

<BaseLayout
	title="About On Deck - an initiative tracker for D&D"
	description="Initiative tracker"
>
<section 
	class="about-section"
	aria-labelledby="about-title"
>
	<h1 id="about-title">
		About On Deck
	</h1>
		<p>
			When you're running a game in Dungeons & Dragons, there are a lot of things you need to keep track of: 
			rules, lore, ensuring everyone is having a good time, and space out snack breaks to keep up morale. 
		</p>
		<p>
			During combat, there are <span class="italic">even more</span> moving parts than usual - 
			Open Deck is a tool that can help reduce cognitive load during gameplay so the DM can focus on 
			storytelling and player experience. 
		</p>
		<p>
			On Deck keeps track of initiative order, turns and rounds, as well as the health of player characters 
			and monsters. It also has a timer function to help you space out breaks.
		</p>
		<p>
			On Deck is using the <a href="https://www.dnd5eapi.co/">D&D 5e API</a> for monster data to 
			automagically fill in HP and AC when adding monsters to encounters.
		</p>
	</section>
	<section 
		class="more-section"
		aria-labelledby="dev-title"
	>
		<h2 id="dev-title">About the dev</h2>
		<p>
			On Deck is made by Maria Jonasson, and I'm a front-end developer student at Medieinstitutet. Open Deck is my degree project.
		</p>
		<p>
			You're welcome to check out the <a href="https://github.com/maria-jon/on-deck">repo on GitHub</a> 
			or head over to <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/maria-jonasson-a4ba24115/">connect with me on LinkedIn</a>.
		</p>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>

<style lang="scss">
	.about-section {
		p {
			margin: var(--margin-lg);
		}

	}

	.more-section {
		margin: var(--margin-xl) var(--margin-md) 0;
		background-color: var(--gold);
		padding: var(--margin-md);
		color: var(--gold-darker);
		border-radius: var(--radius-sm);

		h2 {
			font-size: 2em;
			margin: 0;
		}

		p {
			margin: var(--margin-lg);
		}
		
		a {
			color: var(--blue-darker);
		}

		a:hover {
			color: var(--blue-dark);
		}
	}
</style>